# Change of value (§13): subscriptions, their cancellation, and the
# notifications they bring.

# Process 1 watches analog-input 1, unconfirmed, for 300 s; then cancels.
00 05 01 05 09 01 1c 00 00 00 01 29 00 3a 01 2c => subscribe-cov process 1 analog-input:1 confirmed false lifetime 300
00 05 02 05 09 01 1c 00 00 00 01 => subscribe-cov process 1 analog-input:1 cancel
# One property, confirmed, reporting moves of 0.5 or more.
00 05 03 1c 09 02 1c 00 00 00 01 29 01 3a 01 2c 4e 09 55 4f 5c 3f 00 00 00 => subscribe-cov-property process 2 analog-input:1 confirmed true lifetime 300 property present-value increment 0.5
# What the device sends: present-value and status-flags, unconfirmed with
# an indefinite subscription, confirmed with 290 s left.
10 02 09 01 1c 02 00 02 57 2c 00 00 00 01 39 00 4e 09 55 2e 44 41 ac 00 00 2f 09 6f 2e 82 04 00 2f 4f => cov-notification unconfirmed process 1 device:599 analog-input:1 remaining 0: present-value = real 21.5, status-flags = bits 0000
00 05 07 01 09 01 1c 02 00 02 57 2c 00 00 00 01 3a 01 22 4e 09 55 2e 44 41 ac 00 00 2f 4f => cov-notification confirmed process 1 device:599 analog-input:1 remaining 290: present-value = real 21.5
# A device that does not do COV: optional-functionality-not-supported (45).
50 08 05 91 05 91 2d => error subscribe-cov: services: optional-functionality-not-supported
00 05 09 05 09 01 => error missing-field 1
